{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1786504424,"nonce":"KCdO1HpK1P7epXhC9urFq3sSzxg=","title":"A failed `ingest_batch` is terminal and nothing outside the accept transaction can enqueue a replay","was":"**What is wrong.** The processing path is deliberately built to be replayed, and nothing can trigger a replay. `ingest.process_batch` is enqueued from exactly one place in the codebase — `internal/ingestion/service/accept.go:228`, inside the accept transaction that first received the payload. `cmd/oto` accepts six subcommands and none of them is a replay: `serve` (the default), `api`, `worker`, `migrate`, `bootstrap`, `version` (`cmd/oto/main.go:178-197`). No `operationId` in `api/openapi/openapi.yaml` mentions replay. The only way a stored batch is ever processed is the transaction that accepted it."}]}